        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm identifying the root गुड् in the kutādi group, meaning रक्षायाम् (to protect). The anunasika marker on the अ indicates it's not इदित्, and this group belongs with गाङ्कुटादि where affixes other than ञित् get ङित् treatment.\n\nFor लुङ् (aorist), parasmaipada, this is सेट् with इट् augment. Since it's kutādi, ङित्वत् blocks guna of the उपधा, so the second person plural form becomes अगुडिष्ट — building it as अ + गुड् + इ + स् + त. Vṛddhi doesn't apply here since the root ends in उ, not a halanta consonant, so the final form is अगुडिष्ट.\n\n",
